      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "Open problem: d-bar distance bound for commuting versus general equivariant kernels",
      "body": "OPEN PROBLEM (source_says_open; current status unverified; result status attempted_unsolved). For Gamma-equivariant positive contractions Q, Q' the bound d-bar(P_Q, P_{Q'}) <= 6 3^{2/3} ||Q - Q'||_1^{1/3} holds, and d-bar(P_Q, P_{Q'}) <= ||Q - Q'||_1 when Q and Q' commute. Does the linear bound d-bar <= ||Q - Q'||_1 hold for all pairs? Source: Lyons: Determinantal probability, basic properties and conjectures, ICM 2014, Section 5.2, p. 23.\nPosed in Lyons: Determinantal probability, basic properties and conjectures, ICM 2014\nCurrent status unverified as of 2026-09-07",
